osts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-03T10:42:44-08:00","id":329403,"title":"","content":"...I can't find the shipping costs for standard pledges actually. It's making me a little nervous, since I'm one of those international backer types.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-03T10:51:59-08:00","id":329413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/321472-wraith-20th-ks-12-noon-est-tuesday-december-2nd?p=329403#post329403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...I can't find the shipping costs for standard pledges actually. It's making me a little nervous, since I'm one of those international backer types.</div> </div> </div> </div>When you click on a reward with a print book, the shipping cost's automatically added to the amount of the reward based on where you are, and you can change the location if you need to. The baseline looks to be $25.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-03T12:36:38-08:00","id":329475,"title":"","content":"I REALLY hope we will get a Soulforged Edition. I don't like the black leather used for the cover of the &quot;common&quot; edition of the deluxe books...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2518-erasculio","name":"Erasculio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2518_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-03T12:57:30-08:00","id":329483,"title":"","content":"Kicked in my $85.............now I wait.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-03T14:21:57-08:00","id":329547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/321472-wraith-20th-ks-12-noon-est-tuesday-december-2nd?p=329413#post329413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When you click on a reward with a print book, the shipping cost's automatically added to the amount of the reward based on where you are, and you can change the location if you need to. The baseline looks to be $25.</div> </div> </div> </div>I tried that. It still didn't add anything, listing the shipping total as $0.00. I'm hoping it's because I sprung for one of those higher 'limited run' pledges. But yeah, not comfortable with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-03T21:03:12-08:00","id":329858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RealDeadguy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/321472-wraith-20th-ks-12-noon-est-tuesday-december-2nd?p=328884#post328884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The feedback I got was that while people liked basic Arcanos powers, the bookkeeping was too strenuous and character sheets got overwhelmed by buffet-style sampling. So a lot of them are being folded into 1 dot powers, and there will be further discussion of where we're going with the Ancient/Modern arts over on the KS page in the near future.<br /> <br /> Can't spoil /all/ the secrets yet now, can I?</div> </div> </div> </div>I just hope the Guilds have actual secret Arcanoi uses that are distinctly their's. Otherwise I'm a bit unclear on what their function is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-03T22:03:12-08:00","id":329876,"title":"","content":"I cannot express how excited I am about this kickstarter and happy to see it doing so well, which is obvious since I started the thread &quot;Why I Love Wraith the Oblivion.&quot; I am holding my Oboli back, however, since the tier I wanted to buy into was bought out before I had a chance. Of course I was totally crushed.<br /> <br /> I hope they open up more availability or create new interesting tiers. For those who already are long term Wraith fans and have all the books, the tiers still available (which are marvelous for people just getting into it) leaves us only with the need to buy at the physical book level, leaving much Oboli on the table and not just mine.<br /> <br /> If no other options become available, then I'll just opt for the book.<br /> <br /> I know I'm not the only hard core fan in that position.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1343,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1343-khaleesi","user":"Khaleesi","date":". 12-04-2014, 01:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1343-khaleesi","name":"Khaleesi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T10:30:10-08:00","id":330309,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://www.escapistmagazine.com/articles/view/tabletop/columns/thegauntlett/12709-Wraith-The-Oblivion-Returns-With-Wraith-20th-Anniversary-Kicksta\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.escapistmagazine.com/arti...ersary-Kicksta</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T15:34:41-08:00","id":330567,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">$130,152!</span><br /> <br /> Next. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T19:58:08-08:00","id":330723,"title":"","content":"On one hand, I'm overjoyed that this is doing so well and that we got Orpheus wordcount. On the other, I'm anxiously awaiting Wr20's handling of other Dark Kingdoms; saying &quot;people of different cultures have fundamentally different souls&quot; is problematic, to say the least, and I'd like to see that (along with the particularly racist &quot;Africa's underworld is a pulp stereotype bushland with no culture beyond small tribes&quot;) finally get the boot. V20 gives me hope (look at how far the Ravnos have come, fuck-ups in Open Development aside), but I'm nervous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T20:08:55-08:00","id":330730,"title":"","content":"I'm impressed. I didn't know that many people played Wraith. I've never met anyone face to face who's ever played it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2197-roleplayrose","name":"roleplayrose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2197_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T20:38:07-08:00","id":330736,"title":"","content":"I'm ecstatic that the kickstarter is going so well. Wraith is my favorite game ever and I can't wait to get ahold of a new edition <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> That said, I'm a little bit anxious. Does anyone know why the projected page count is so much smaller than V20, W20 and M20? :/","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/79-alexisvalarr","name":"alexisvalarr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar79_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T21:00:16-08:00","id":330746,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\">My best guess on the page count: Mr. D\u2019s Circle hasn\u2019t finished the entire book so they\u2019re probably spit-balling a page count. <br /> <br /> Without comparing to the other X20s, Wraith Second was a hair under 300 pages. Adding the juicy tidbits about all the Arcanoi, the Legions, Risen, Spectres, Dark Kingdoms, Orpheus, etc., will probably push it over. Those extra 30-50 pages from Orpheus will also add some width. <br /> <br /> Overall, I wouldn\u2019t sweat the whole \u201c300\u201d thing. <br /> Unless you're Xerxes. <br /> Then definitely sweat it. (<span style=\"font-size:8px\">\u201cThis is STYGIA!\u201d)</span> </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T21:59:28-08:00","id":330758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/321472-wraith-20th-ks-12-noon-est-tuesday-december-2nd?p=330723#post330723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On one hand, I'm overjoyed that this is doing so well and that we got Orpheus wordcount. On the other, I'm anxiously awaiting Wr20's handling of other Dark Kingdoms; saying &quot;people of different cultures have fundamentally different souls&quot; is problematic, to say the least, and I'd like to see that (along with the particularly racist &quot;Africa's underworld is a pulp stereotype bushland with no culture beyond small tribes&quot;) finally get the boot. V20 gives me hope (look at how far the Ravnos have come, fuck-ups in Open Development aside), but I'm nervous.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> and DA20 gives Hope on how foreign things can exist that disprove &quot;stuff everyone knows&quot; without turning all the other dark kingdoms into lands of funny hats.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T22:02:50-08:00","id":330759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>roleplayrose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/321472-wraith-20th-ks-12-noon-est-tuesday-december-2nd?p=330730#post330730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm impressed. I didn't know that many people played Wraith. I've never met anyone face to face who's ever played it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't played it. I just really want too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T22:07:13-08:00","id":330760,"title":"","content":"Actually, I will make the confession that I skipped over pretty much all of the Dark Kingdoms bits in the old books as I don't feel I ever really understood them well, and was never really drawn to play them. I can't comment on how racist they are (different areas don't have different souls so much as different parts of the Underworld operate by different rules, much like different realms of the Umbra or the Astral plane have different rules) but that's mostly because I can't even remember 90% of that material. So really I just hope the Dark Kingdoms will be a little less alien seeming and a little easier to comprehend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T23:33:43-08:00","id":330836,"title":"","content":"Perhaps of note for those worried about the Dark Kingdoms is <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=171742#post171742\">Rich Dansky's view</a> of what the Dark Kingdoms are.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Dark Kingdoms are built on a combination of dominant cultural paradigm, ability to find &amp; hold territory in the Underworld, and occasional bits of plain luck. The major powers have secured major real estate; that's not to say there aren't outposts of wraiths who came out of a different culture who interact with the afterlife in their own way, trying to carve out their own territory here and there. Of course, that sort of existence isn't likely to make them friendly to outsiders. As for the Dark Kingdom of Wire, that name is bitterly ironic, and the entity it describes exists within Stygia's borders. </div> </div> </div>Backing up what he says about dominant cultural paradigm, according to Wraith: The Great War, wraiths from other Dark Kingdoms can take on the Stygian soul-structure of Psyche-Shadow if they remain in Stygian territory for prolonged periods of time<i>. </i>It's the cultural paradigm that shapes soul-structure in the Underworld, not any fundamental difference in the souls themselves.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-06T00:17:50-08:00","id":332011,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">$140,355!</span><br /> <br /> Next up, <i>Handbook for the Recently Deceased</i>!</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-06T00:41:30-08:00","id":332020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nazfool</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/321472-wraith-20th-ks-12-noon-est-tuesday-december-2nd?p=330746#post330746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><br /> Overall, I wouldn\u2019t sweat the whole \u201c300\u201d thing.<br /> Unless you're Xerxes.<br /> Then definitely sweat it. (<span style=\"font-size:8px\">\u201cThis is STYGIA!\u201d)</span> </span></div> </div> </div> </div>When I read that I was thinking of a totally different Xerxes. But then, I guess we don't talk about him in Wraith threads. &gt;.&gt;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-06T00:58:07-08:00","id":332023,"title":"","content":"...Nukes are not toys for playing with.<br /> <br /> Stupid, silly technocrat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-06T06:37:12-08:00","id":332177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/321472-wraith-20th-ks-12-noon-est-tuesday-december-2nd?p=332023#post332023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Nukes are not toys for playing with.<br /> <br /> Stupid, silly technocrat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically it wasn't his fault. His nuke was prematurely set off by the Smiling Lord nuking Enoch which happened because they were besieging Enoch at the request of the Ferrymen who were forced to because of an ancient debt they owed to Anubis. So really, its the fault of Anubis and his schemes and possibly also the Smiling Lord's heavyhanded tactics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-07T08:12:39-08:00","id":332967,"title":"","content":"I am conflicted about this.<br /> <br /> On one hand I want it and I have faith in Rich Dansky, on the other hand I am so fucking pissed at how Onyx Path has been handling the <b>Exalted</b> Kickstarter and I have little faith in Rich Thomas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.redbubble.com/people/nesling/works/15673780-loch-ness-monster-on-vacation?c=409846-mixed&amp;p=throw-pillow\" target=\"_blank\">Loch Ness monsters. On vacation. On a pillow.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> My wife is on <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1Ngo336SKXWmoRnG3QWmhS\" target=\"_blank\">Spotify</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/864-jutlander","name":"Jutlander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-07T08:41:35-08:00","id":333005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jutlander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/321472-wraith-20th-ks-12-noon-est-tuesday-december-2nd?p=332967#post332967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am conflicted about this.<br /> <br /> On one hand I want it and I have faith in Rich Dansky, on the other hand I am so fucking pissed at how Onyx Path has been handling the <b>Exalted</b> Kickstarter and I have little faith in Rich Thomas.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well to be fair every other KS they're run have been pretty good and OPP has gotten a much better handle on running KS since Exalted 3E.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-07T13:11:03-08:00","id":333311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jutlander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/321472-wraith-20th-ks-12-noon-est-tuesday-december-2nd?p=332967#post332967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am conflicted about this.<br /> <br /> On one hand I want it and I have faith in Rich Dansky, on the other hand I am so fucking pissed at how Onyx Path has been handling the <b>Exalted</b> Kickstarter and I have little faith in Rich Thomas.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? In what way have I let you down, Jutlander?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-07T13:39:30-08:00","id":333348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jutlander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/321472-wraith-20th-ks-12-noon-est-tuesday-december-2nd?p=332967#post332967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am conflicted about this.<br /> <br /> On one hand I want it and I have faith in Rich Dansky, on the other hand I am so fucking pissed at how Onyx Path has been handling the <b>Exalted</b> Kickstarter and I have little faith in Rich Thomas.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> On of the main writers have faced serious illness - and a huge portion needed rewriting so it would not become a bogged down slow puddle of a game like the last two editions. The game is coming - it is in development and that is what KS paid for. One should actually ignore the Dates the whole way. <br /> Would I like to have that book in my hands now, OH yes, very much - had actually hoped having a year gaming with it till now. Is it irritating it takes so much longer, mhm. Does that make me loose fate in the developers? No.<br /> So I am waiting, having fun leading my other rpg's and hoping a brand new totally reinvisioned game is landing in my mailbox next year and much sooner in my electronic mailbox.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1159-kjetilkverndokken","name":"kjetilkverndokken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1159_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-07T14:02:34-08:00","id":333370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RichT</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/321472-wraith-20th-ks-12-noon-est-tuesday-december-2nd?p=333311#post333311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really? In what way have I let you down, Jutlander?</div> </div> </div> </div>You are not really surprised that people feel let down by the <b>Exalted</b> Kickstarter, are you?<br /> <br /> The first and most major problem is the endless delays. The third edition of <b>Exalted</b> was first announced to come out in 2012. We are now entering 2015. Even if we go by the date announced in the Kickstarter, the game is very late. It should not be a surprise that this upsets people for a variety of reasons. Apart from having lost interest in the game to the point where I have sold most of my books, I hurts me personally because I bought two books - one for myself and one as a baptism present for the child of my first <b>Exalted </b>storyteller. That child is more than a year old now.<br /> <br /> The second reason is the communication surrounding the delays as well as the content of the book. It has gotten better, but it has not been good. At all. It has been very limited what we were told and the developers have come off as patronising and dismissive. And that is not even bringing up Holden's unfortunate comments about rape.<br /> <br /> Thirdly, you are allowing the head developer to use the name of the company and of the game as he begs for money publicly for his medical bills? I am not a big fan of that to say the least. I wish John M\u00f8rke all the best and he has my sympathy, but it comes off as if he is holding the game hostage. It should never be the responsibility of the fans to pay for the medical bills of a person hired to do a product they have already paid for (and that is already very late). Of course, you cannot tell him not to beg, but you can tell him not to use the company and product names while doing so as it reflects poorly upon you.<br /> <br /> Finally, and I know this is a matter of taste, I am not a big fan of the product we have seen so far. The comic is all about a character who is solely important not due to his own powers but due to the capabilities of a man who dies 1,500 years ago (which we are told about in a long-winded flashback). This goes against the themes and feel of the new edition of the game, unless I have been misinterpreting what little information we have.<br /> <br /> It cannot be a surprise to you that the delays and poor communication, at least, have been a letdown.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.redbubble.com/people/nesling/works/15673780-loch-ness-monster-on-vacation?c=409846-mixed&amp;p=throw-pillow\" target=\"_blank\">Loch Ness monsters. On vacation. On a pillow.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> My wife is on <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1Ngo336SKXWmoRnG3QWmhS\" target=\"_blank\">Spotify</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/864-jutlander","name":"Jutlander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-07T16:28:11-08:00","id":333555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/321472-wraith-20th-ks-12-noon-est-tuesday-december-2nd?p=329858#post329858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I just hope the Guilds have actual secret Arcanoi uses that are distinctly their's. (...)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This. Rich D, This. <br /> <br /> To my own post now.<br /> <br /> Thanks for making this project happen, Wraith is my favorite setting too! (although I admit to making a near 30 pages adaptation booklet of the metaplot and some mechanics for the LARP project I'm organizing :P)<br /> <br /> Question: This is my first KS, so this is probably trivial. Still. Can I pledge for a reward and add $1 to have a different name on the badass &quot;Army of the Night&quot; section additionally to my &quot;Wraith&quot; name? or even a number of $1 entries, all in one transaction? A single reward pledge would reduce international card transaction fees for me, which would be $ going down the Nihil. I plan to add the $5 fiction books add-on too, so the total would be needing clarification.<br /> <br /> My opinion on the stretch goals: the jumps between them are a liiitle too much aren't they? i haven't followed the previous KS projects, but 40k for a stretch goal does fuel my shadow with the bad kind of Angst. I'm not a developer so do say how wrong I am (if you care to reply), but making like a 5k jump for a new fiction and a 10k jump to content on the Wr20 sounds linear/plausible to me. <br /> <br /> For the cover, if you can make the eerie glow and rough surface like the first edition, I believe that would be an awesome touch for a 20th Deluxe Edition.<br /> <br /> My 2 Oboli.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4474-ivarov","name":"Ivarov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4474_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-07T18:40:29-08:00","id":333654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ivarov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/321472-wraith-20th-ks-12-noon-est-tuesday-december-2nd?p=333555#post333555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Question: This is my first KS, so this is probably trivial. Still. Can I pledge for a reward and add $1 to have a different name on the badass &amp;quot;Army of the Night&amp;quot; section additionally to my &amp;quot;Wraith&amp;quot; name? or even a number of $1 entries, all in one transaction? A single reward pledge would reduce international card transaction fees for me, which would be $ going down the Nihil. I plan to add the $5 fiction books add-on too, so the total would be needing clarification.<br /> <br /> My opinion on the stretch goals: the jumps between them are a liiitle too much aren't they? i haven't followed the previous KS projects, but 40k for a stretch goal does fuel my shadow with the bad kind of Angst. I'm not a developer so do say how wrong I am (if you care to reply), but making like a 5k jump for a new fiction and a 10k jump to content on the Wr20 sounds linear/plausible to me. </div> </div> </div> </div>The only way to get more names is to pledge for additional Reward Tiers. There's no Add-on to get more names in there.<br /> <br /> If you haven't yet, please read through the comments section of the Wraith20 KS where I respond about Stretch Goals amounts. For briefly, the amounts to activate stretch goals are not &quot;free money&quot;. Most of those funds are committed to the same creation and shipping of physical rewards, the book and screen, as any other bunch of pledges. What little remains after Kickstarter, Amazon Payments, and CCP fees, we decide to spend on the creation of stretch goal rewards. In the case of the Orpheus addition, that means an entire new chapter's worth of writing, development, art, layout, and the accompanying costs to create all that- plus the added cost for adding more pages to be printed, and a larger weight when shipping. It is no small addition and costs a bunch- hence that goal amount, which is very little compared to other Kickstarters out there. Hope that helps.<br /> <br /> Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-07T18:57:28-08:00","id":333664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RichT</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/321472-wraith-20th-ks-12-noon-est-tuesday-december-2nd?p=333654#post333654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The only way to get more names is to pledge for additional Reward Tiers. There's no Add-on to get more names in there.<br /> <br /> If you haven't yet, please read through the comments section of the Wraith20 KS where I respond about Stretch Goals amounts. For briefly, the amounts to activate stretch goals are not &quot;free money&quot;. Most of those funds are committed to the same creation and shipping of physical rewards, the book and screen, as any other bunch of pledges. What little remains after Kickstarter, Amazon Payments, and CCP fees, we decide to spend on the creation of stretch goal rewards. In the case of the Orpheus addition, that means an entire new chapter's worth of writing, development, art, layout, and the accompanying costs to create all that- plus the added cost for adding more pages to be printed, and a larger weight when shipping. It is no small addition and costs a bunch- hence that goal amount, which is very little compared to other Kickstarters out there. Hope that helps.<br /> <br /> Thanks!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 'Appreciate the fast reply. I've read some of the comments on KS page, no doubt missed that bit. I believe Wraith (and crew) deserves way more than 150k, so I hope by the end of the month it reaches at the very least triple of what it is today, so dont get my comment as mingy/iron-fisted, its just that, as a player, MOAR CONTENT, y'know <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4474-ivarov","name":"Ivarov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4474_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-07T20:26:39-08:00","id":333700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jutlander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/321472-wraith-20th-ks-12-noon-est-tuesday-december-2nd?p=332967#post332967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am conflicted about this.<br /> <br /> On one hand I want it and I have faith in Rich Dansky, on the other hand I am so fucking pissed at how Onyx Path has been handling the <b>Exalted</b> Kickstarter and I have little faith in Rich Thomas.</div> </div> </div> </div>So when is the head person in charge of Wraith20 going to get seriously ill and when are they going to completely rewrite the CWoD Storyteller system?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T12:10:21-08:00","id":334408,"title":"","content":"I wanna say I'm really happy Wraith 20th is getting so much support. It's a game I love so much and I think it really deserve all the fan support <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> But I have to say I don't understand very well some things of this Kickstarter:<br /> <br /> First, the 300+ problem. V20, W20 and M20 have been 500+ books, a 300+ is an old rulebook not a big special compendium with all the info of several rulebooks and supplements.<br /> Second, if Wraith is getting a book with 200 pages less than other 20th editions, why its price (110$) is almost the same than W20 (120$) or M20 (135$)?<br /> And third, the stretchgoals. I love we are gonna getting Dark Kingdom of Jade Arcanoi, but why that's a stretchgoal? V20 had every Discipline, I really thought we'd get every Arcanoi in Wraith20 without discussion, from the very beginning, no like a goal that perhaps we wouldn't get. I was waiting other kind of stretchgoals, like new info for future books (in the M20 KS style).<br /> <br /> I really hope noone missunderstand me. I'm trully thankful to Onyx Path for bringing back cWoD for all of us, and to Mr. Dansky for all his work (you can't imagine how much I've enjoyed your old work for Wraith and how much I wanna read the new book), but these things make me feel that (for some unknown reason) Wraith fans deserve less than other WoD fans and that makes me really sad (and give me some Angst points).<br /> I only can hope Ultradeluxe edition gives me some happy Pathos, at least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/n6g3njp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/kpa5GS5Mp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/93820aaad7.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/584-eliseo-ap-liam","name":"Eliseo ap Liam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar584_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T12:50:23-08:00","id":334450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/321472-wraith-20th-ks-12-noon-est-tuesday-december-2nd?p=333700#post333700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So when is the head person in charge of Wraith20 going to get seriously ill and when are they going to completely rewrite the CWoD Storyteller system?</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't ask that in front of The Wraith Curse!<br /> <br /> As for your thoughts, Jutlander, of course I understand anyone waiting for EX3 who might feel disappointed, or frustrated, or angry about how long things have taken. What I have tried to do from the Kickstarter onward is to keep everyone involved informed with the decisions we have been making and the progress, or lack thereof, we've made. Pretty much every time I've learned any new info, I've alerted backers and the rest of the EX community on our various platforms.<br /> <br /> At the same time, we've improved and evolved our Kickstarter methods to insure that the pitfalls we fell into with the EX3 KS don't happen again, and I think we've made a lot of changes for the better. Each project is different, as is each Kickstarter, and each one has different challenges. Similarly, what works really well with one project, with it's particular fan-base and creators, doesn't necessarily port over to a different project and it's specific fans and creators. We've managed to distill a lot of what works well across projects, but yeah, we're still experimenting and learning as we go.<br /> <br /> As for communication, I wonder if you are referring to the info I personally am able to pass on to you, as I mentioned above, in which case I can only say that I've also had folks tell me how great the communication has been for their needs or compared to other KSs, or who complained that I was &quot;spamming their inboxes&quot; with too many Updates that don't just say the book is done. So clearly communication is something that folks have different ideas about, and I'm sorry if I was not able to meets your needs there. If you are instead wishing for more excerpts from EX3 in Updates, then that again comes down to the comfort level of the creative team with what is shown to the community, and when. I'm not going to rip a chunk of text out of their current files and slap it up there unless we all agree internally that it is the thing to do.<br /> <br /> A lot of people think that because one of our creators is working for Onyx Path that we have some sort of power over the personal behavior and messaging. We don't, and in fact there are some pretty significant differences between what I can ask of the vast majority of our teams who are all freelancers, and the other two people besides myself who are employed by Onyx Path. I can ask, and do, when the way they have phrased something implies that their words comes from some sort of official Onyx Path approved position and it isn't that, and every time so far that I've had to, the freelancer has changed the message. That happened with John's medical crowdfunding efforts, and he was quick to pull the stuff that made it seem like Onyx Path was involved. Maybe you missed that if you didn't recheck his messaging.<br /> <br /> Finally, sorry you didn't like the comic. The Devs worked hand in glove with Zub and Hanzo, so I'm pretty sure the story was as they expected it to be.<br /> <br /> Appreciate you writing out your concerns!<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T13:05:41-08:00","id":334466,"title":"","content":"...<br /> <br /> I don't envy Rich's position, as he has to continually explain the same things.<br /> <br /> Over, and over, and over, and over, and over and over, and over again. <br /> <br /> The wait for Exalted 3 has sucked. Royally. But Onyx Path HAS delivered on every single thing they've promised so far(except for V20 Red List : ), and each deluxe edition has been amazing. I have no doubt that Exalted will deliver when it's finally released.<br /> <br /> They've also made changes for the good, thanks to consumer feedback. Future scheduling was one of them. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T16:13:24-08:00","id":334628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RichT</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/321472-wraith-20th-ks-12-noon-est-tuesday-december-2nd?p=334450#post334450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Appreciate you writing out your concerns!</div> </div> </div> </div>And I appreciate you taking the time to answer in a respectful, acknowledging, and cohesive manner. Thank you for that.<br /> <br /> Most of my issues are with the <b>Exalted </b>developers and not really with you, I guess. I will be brief:<br /> <br /> 1) I appreciate you acknowledging the negative feelings of me and many other backers. I am still really frustrated about the whole thing, but this helps.<br /> <br /> 2) I was referring to the communication by the two developers.<br /> <br /> 3) I had not seen that his message was changed, but I appreciate that it was.<br /> <br /> 4) I don't like it and I don't understand, or agree with, the choices made by the developers. Would I be frustrated by it if the game had not been delayed? Not as much, I guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.redbubble.com/people/nesling/works/15673780-loch-ness-monster-on-vacation?c=409846-mixed&amp;p=throw-pillow\" target=\"_blank\">Loch Ness monsters. On vacation. On a pillow.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> My wife is on <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1Ngo336SKXWmoRnG3QWmhS\" target=\"_blank\">Spotify</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/864-jutlander","name":"Jutlander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-10T19:36:03-08:00","id":336602,"title":"","content":"So, Rich, Wraith 20th: Soulforged Edition? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\"